 61CR c  2020On01: {+61}V beam produced from fragmentation of 140 MeV/nucleon   
 61CR2c  {+82}Se beam on {+9}Be target, followed by mass separation by A1900    
 61CR3c  separator at NSCL-MSU accelerator facility. The resulting cocktail     
 61CR4c  ion beam was transported to the Beta Counting System and implanted     
 61CR5c  into a double-sided silicon strip detector. Measured |b-delayed        
 61CR6c  neutrons in coincidence with |b particles, and total absorption |g-ray 
 61CR7c  spectrum in coincidence with |b particles using the neutron long       
 61CR8c  counter system NERO for neutrons, and SuN detector for the |g          
 61CR9c  radiation. Deduced |b feedings to the ground and excited states,       
 61CRAc  and in the continuum together with beta-delayed neutron emission       
 61CRBc  probability %|b{+-}n or Pn, B(>) strengths, and Urca neutrino cooling  
 61CRCc  contribution from A=55, 57, 59, 61, 63, and 65 decays for a neutron    
 61CRDc  star crust from the rp-process. Comparison with QRPA-fy theoretical    
 61CREc  calculations                                                           
